@1017 = ~Javelins are typically light, flexible spears designed primarily as a throwing weapon. However the Iron Elegy weghs heavy in your hands due to its iron shaft and steel tip. 

Mubark was a half-ogre who dwelled near the Forest of Tethir. After a dispute with a local cleric who tried to drive Mubark from the land, Mubark commissioned the Elegy to counter the cleric's magic and was able to defend his home from further incursions.

STATISTICS:

Combat Abilities: Javelin returns to the wielder's hand instantly after an attack is made
Combat Ability (10% of hits): Save vs. spell or Silenced for two rounds
THAC0:  +2 bonus
Damage: 1d%ranged_die% + 2 (thrown, missile)
Damage: 1d%melee_die% + 2 (melee, piercing)
Weight: 15
Speed Factor: 2
Proficiency Type: Spear 
Type:  1-handed
Requires: 12 Strength
Not Usable By:
 Cleric
 Mage
 Thief~
@1020 = ~Javelins are light, flexible spears designed primarily as a throwing weapon. They are usually constructed of wood and tipped with a small metal spearhead. The shaft is much thinner than a two-handed spear. The javelin is a ranged weapon, intended to be thrown. While javelins can be used for melee combat, they are not sturdy enough and perform poorly.

The javelin of fire is a magical javelin that will burst into flames as it is fired at an enemy. The effect is similar to a javelin doused in oil and set to flame.

STATISTICS:

THAC0:  +1 bonus
Damage: 1d%ranged_die% + 1 (thrown, missile)
Damage: 1d%melee_die% + 1 (melee, piercing)
Special:  1D4 fire damage (save vs. spell for none)
Weight: 2
Speed Factor: 3
Proficiency Type: Spear 
Type:  1-handed
Requires: 5 Strength
Not Usable By:
 Cleric
 Mage
 Thief~